---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.ts';
---

<Base
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description={`How ${site.name} is funded, what is and is not an affiliate link, and that commissions do not change calculator output or the spec library.`}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Affiliate disclosure</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-400">Last updated: {site.legalUpdated}.</p>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      This page is the material-connection disclosure for {site.name}. It is linked from every
      footer. When a retailer checkout link exists, a short notice will also sit next to that link.
      The rule is the FTC's Endorsement Guides: if a commission is possible, say so where a reader
      can see it before they click.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Current status</h2>
    {
      site.affiliateLive ? (
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
          Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you follow one and buy, we may earn a
          commission at no extra cost to you. The calculator still filters on published
          specifications. We do not accept payment for placement.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
            No affiliate links and no retailer checkout links are live. Station pages name the
            manufacturer product page as the source. Those outbound links use rel="nofollow
            noopener". They are citations, not store buttons.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
            If a program later approves this site, three things will happen in the same deploy:
            checkout links may appear on model pages, this page will name the program, and the
            footer will add a short notice that some links may be affiliate links. Until that
            deploy, there is nothing to disclose beyond this status.
          </p>
        </>
      )
    }

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What a commission will not change</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Whether or not a link exists, these stay independent of payment:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        Calculator output. Runtime and recommended capacity use the same formula on the
        <a class="underline" href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        Which models appear. A record ships only when a person has read the manufacturer page named
        in its source URL.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        Whether a boost rating is treated as inverter surge. It is not. A motor start is not cleared
        by X-Boost, Power Lifting, SurgePad, or any other resistive boost name.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">Paid placement. We do not accept payment to add, rank, or hide a model.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What this site will not add</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      We do not provide price history, price-drop alerts, or marketplace price curves. Manufacturer
      list prices, when shown, are dated figures from the source page, not live offers. Program
      requirements will be checked before any affiliate integration is enabled.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      We do not run "official store" language for a brand we do not operate. Brand names identify
      products.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How to read a link, when links exist</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      A manufacturer source URL is a citation. An affiliate checkout URL, if one is added, will be
      labeled as such next to the control. Until then, there is no checkout control to label.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Questions</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Email
      <!--email_off--><a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a><!--/email_off-->.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
